{"source_clause": "(b) Wages

For purposes of this chapter, the term "wages" means all remuneration for employment, including the cash value of all remuneration (including benefits) paid in any medium other than cash; except that such term shall not include-

    (1) that part of the remuneration which, after remuneration (other than remuneration referred to in the succeeding paragraphs of this subsection) equal to $7,000 with respect to employment has been paid to an individual by an employer during any calendar year, is paid to such individual by such employer during such calendar year;

    ", "local_scope": "Compute the local amount inclusion specified by3306(b)(1). Other statutory exclusions are outside this component. No complete3306 predictor is requested.", "input_relation": {"admitted_payments": {"columns": ["payment_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY", "payer TEXT", "payee TEXT", "payment_year INTEGER", "service_id TEXT", "amount INTEGER"], "meaning": "Each row is one physical direct payment of nonnegative gross remuneration by the payer/employer to the payee/individual in payment_year. An ordinary input adapter admits it when any supplied candidate-admission witness exists and emits it once. Different payment IDs remain different payments even when amounts coincide. This shared adapter is given to both controls, not learned from the law."}}, "scope_and_operation_language_identical_for_SQL_and_plan": {"cap": "Group by the chosen scope keys, sum amount inside each group, include min(threshold,group sum), then sum included amounts.", "exclude_scope_at_least": "Group by the chosen scope keys; include0 for a group whose sum>=threshold, otherwise include its whole sum; sum the included values.", "exclude_scope_above": "Same whole-group exclusion with > instead of >=.", "include_all": "Include each group total without applying the threshold."}, "scope_semantics": "Each distinct tuple of selected keys is one scope. payment_id in the keys permits per-payment scopes; an empty key list is one global scope. Choose the legal keys and operation from the source, not from a fixed expected answer.", "source_contract_counterexamples": [{"name": "empty", "admitted_payments": [], "source_required_total": 0}, {"name": "annual_same_person_two_payments", "admitted_payments": [["a", "P", "Q", 2017, "S", 6771], ["b", "P", "Q", 2017, "S", 6954]], "source_required_total": 7000}, {"name": "different_payers", "admitted_payments": [["a", "P", "Q", 2017, "S", 7000], ["b", "R", "Q", 2017, "S", 7000]], "source_required_total": 14000}, {"name": "different_payees", "admitted_payments": [["a", "P", "Q", 2017, "S", 6771], ["b", "P", "R", 2017, "S", 6771]], "source_required_total": 13542}, {"name": "different_payment_years", "admitted_payments": [["a", "P", "Q", 2017, "S", 7000], ["b", "P", "Q", 2018, "S", 7000]], "source_required_total": 14000}, {"name": "same_annual_key_different_services", "admitted_payments": [["a", "P", "Q", 2017, "S", 6771], ["b", "P", "Q", 2017, "T", 6954]], "source_required_total": 7000}, {"name": "same_payment_multiple_witnesses", "admitted_payments": [["a", "P", "Q", 2017, "S", 1000]], "source_required_total": 1000}, {"name": "unqualified_payment_not_counted", "admitted_payments": [["a", "P", "Q", 2017, "S", 1000]], "source_required_total": 1000}], "repair_context": "Previous candidates were rejected. Do NOT copy a previous programme or treat rejected examples as authoritative. The rejected code is intentionally not included here. Re-derive the operation and scope from the source and the shared source-contract examples.", "requested_output": "One integer total; empty input gives0. No original native case facts/query/label, annotated runtime records or reference SQL are supplied. Source-contract examples are explicit shared training feedback, not a native evaluation set."}

law_cache = lambda facts, query: sum(min(7000, sum(p['amount'] for p in group)) for group in (group_by(facts, ['payer', 'payee', 'payment_year']) if query == 'component3306_b_1' else []))

def group_by(data, keys):
    groups = {}
    for item in data:
        key = tuple(item[k] for k in keys)
        if key not in groups:
            groups[key] = []
        groups[key].append(item)
    return groups
